What I understood you are asking for:
1. "Run OTTER with an L1 sparsity penalty of 0.1 so that most TF-gene edges are exactly zero" -- not available here as asked. NetZoo's OTTER has no setting for "L1 sparsity penalty of 0.1"; the settings it passes are output_format, computing, precision, lam, gamma, iterations, eta and bexp. OTTER itself can still run, with its own settings instead -- an alternative, not the setting you asked for.

